A command with two init functions, which share one reference. The second holds a
type error and a dead store, so the type error skips it and its store is not
reported, though the first init, which answers for the reference, type-checks.

-- go.mod --
module example.com/app

go 1.27
-- deadset.json --
{"target": {"kind": "application"}}
-- main.go --
package main

func main() {}

func init() {}

func init() {
	v := 1
	v = 2
	_ = v
	println(undefinedName)
}
